						<div class="postbody"><div class="quotetitle">BigBCanada wrote:</div><div class="quotecontent">Hydrolysates are predigested, partially hydrolyzed whey proteins that, as a consequence, are more easily absorbed, but their cost is generally higher. Highly-hydrolysed whey may be less allergenic than other forms of whey<br /></div>Love my hydro-whey. &lt;3<br /><br />Also, it's nice how it defines whey concentrates.  Beginners/starters may see &quot;includes whey concentrates&quot; and think that's just pure whey right there, while it can really be as low as just 29% whey.</div>

